hostname r3
!
ip routing
!
interface Loopback0
   ip address 10.0.0.3/32
!
interface Ethernet1
   description to r2:eth2
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.23.2/30
!
interface Ethernet2
   description to r4:eth1
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.34.1/30
!
! ============================================================
! YOUR TASKS ON R3
! ============================================================
!
! TASK 1 — Base BGP session
!   configure
!   router bgp 65003
!      bgp router-id 10.0.0.3
!      neighbor 10.1.23.1 remote-as 65002
!      neighbor 10.1.34.2 remote-as 65004
!      !
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.23.1 activate
!         neighbor 10.1.34.2 activate
!         network 10.0.0.3/32
!      !
!
! TASK 2 — Observe the effect of no-export from r1
!   If r1 tagged its loopback with community no-export, r2 should NOT
!   have sent it to r3.
!
!   Check: show bgp ipv4 unicast
!   10.0.0.1/32 should be ABSENT from r3's BGP table.
!
!   Compare: if r2 is receiving it (show bgp ipv4 unicast on r2 shows it),
!   but r3 doesn't have it — the no-export community is working correctly.
!
! TASK 3 — Observe community propagation
!   If r1 sets community 65001:100 (without no-export), r2 forwards it to r3.
!   On r3: show bgp ipv4 unicast 10.0.0.1/32
!   You should see "Community: 65001:100" in the detail output.
!
!   Communities propagate by default to eBGP peers. You must explicitly
!   strip them if you don't want them forwarded.
!
! TASK 4 — Apply your own community policy on r3
!   Match community 65001:100 on routes received from r2, and set local-preference:
!
!   ip community-list standard UPSTREAM-TAG permit 65001:100
!   route-map HONOR-TAG permit 10
!      match community UPSTREAM-TAG
!      set local-preference 150
!   route-map HONOR-TAG permit 20
!
!   router bgp 65003
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.23.1 route-map HONOR-TAG in
!      !
! ============================================================
end
